{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>מחלה</b> — letters of <i>הלחם</i> (bread) and letters of <i>המלח</i> (salt): to teach you that eighty-three kinds of disease depend on the gall, and morning bread with salt and a flask of water annul them. Therefore Scripture juxtaposed to it: עינת מים (springs of water)." "<b>רופאך</b> — the peh is weak (r'fuyah): healing that is in the hands of Heaven comes with ease, and that which is in the hands of man comes with difficulty. Therefore <i>ורפא</i> in the portion of Mishpatim is hard (daghesh)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:09.058259348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}